on skills.\n- weaknesses: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education.\n\nCandidate D:\n- strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously.\n- weaknesses: considered moody, regarded as a loner.\n\nNow evaluate for long-distance pilot.\n\nReliability: C seems reliable (quick correct decisions, concern for others). D takes responsibility seriously. A anticipates dangerous situations (reliability). B conscientious.\n\nTechnical competence: A spatial vision, complex connections (good for navigation). B weather assessment, computer skills. D problem solving, concentration. C attention skills.\n\nCalmness under pressure: B handles stress well. D responds to unexpected events adequately. A anticipates dangerous situations (maybe proactive). C quick decisions.\n\nDecision-making: C quick correct decisions. A anticipates dangerous situations (maybe proactive). D solves problems extremely well.\n\nTeamwork/communication: A leadership qualities but unfriendly. B pretentious, wrong tone. C difficulty communicating, egocentric, but puts concern for others above everything. D loner, moody.\n\nProfessional development: C not willing to further education. B maybe okay. D unknown. A unknown.\n\nWe need to weigh. For long-distance flights, crew coordination is crucial. Communication issues are serious. Candidate C's difficulty communicating and egocentric may be problematic despite concern for others. Candidate B's pretentiousness and wrong tone also problematic. Candidate A unfriendly may affect crew. Candidate D loner/moody may affect crew.\n\nLeadership: A has very good leadership qualities. That is a plus. But unfriendly may hinder.\n\nReliability: C seems reliable. A anticipates dangerous situations (proactive safety). D takes responsibility seriously.\n\nOverall, which candidate balances? Perhaps Candidate A: strong leadership, anticipation, spatial vision, but unfriendly and unhealthy eating (maybe health concerns). Unfriendly could affect crew but leadership may mitigate. Health (eating unhealthily) could affect long flights but not necessarily immediate.\n\nCandidate D: strong problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but moody and loner, weak leadership.\n\nCandidate B: stress handling, weather, conscientious, but pretentious and tone issues.\n\nCandidate C: quick decisions, concern for others, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to develop.\n\nGiven crew coordination is vital, communication difficulty is a big red flag. So maybe B or A. A has leadership, but unfriendly may be less severe than communication difficulty. Also A's anticipation and spatial vision are critical for navigation. So I might lean toward Candidate A, but note uncertainty about unfriendly behavior and health.\n\nThus provisional preference: Candidate A.\n\nWe should mention evidence, alternatives, tradeoffs, uncertainties, what would change vote.\n\nNow produce output."}
